---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro'
import PageHead from '@/components/PageHead.astro'
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout class="max-w-3xl">
  <PageHead slot="head" title="Data Processing Agreement" />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Data Processing Agreement', icon: 'lucide:database' }]} />

  <section class="prose max-w-none">
    <h1>Data Processing Agreement</h1>
    <p class="text-muted-foreground text-sm">Last updated: May 4, 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Data Processing Agreement ("DPA") supplements our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
      and <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> for organizations ("Controller") that use
      Kapisce under an institutional or bulk license and are subject to data protection
      regulations such as GDPR, UK GDPR, or similar laws.
    </p>

    <p>
      To enter into this DPA with Nowispow, Inc ("Processor"), please contact
      <a href="mailto:webmaster@nowispow.com">webmaster@nowispow.com</a>. Execution of a signed
      DPA is required before we can act as a Processor for your organization's user data.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Definitions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Controller</strong> — the organization that determines the purposes and means of
        processing personal data (e.g. a school or library that provides Kapisce access to
        students or patrons).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Processor</strong> — Nowispow, Inc, which processes personal data on behalf of
        the Controller.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Personal Data</strong> — any information relating to an identified or identifiable
        natural person, as defined under applicable data protection law.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Processing</strong> — any operation performed on Personal Data, including
        collection, storage, use, and deletion.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Subject Matter and Duration</h2>
    <p>
      This DPA covers Nowispow's processing of Personal Data on behalf of the Controller in
      connection with the Controller's use of Kapisce's services. Processing continues for the
      duration of the Controller's active license and for any legally required retention period
      thereafter.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Nature and Purpose of Processing</h2>
    <p>Nowispow processes Personal Data for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Managing subscriber records and delivering email communications (Listmonk).</li>
      <li>Collecting anonymised reading-engagement analytics (PostHog, self-hosted).</li>
      <li>Processing payments and delivering license keys (via Lemon Squeezy as MoR).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. Categories of Data Subjects and Personal Data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Email address and role (educator / book-club leader / reader) for subscribers.</li>
      <li>Anonymised or hashed device identifiers for analytics.</li>
      <li>Email address associated with a purchase, for license key delivery.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Processor Obligations</h2>
    <p>Nowispow shall:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Process Personal Data only on documented instructions from the Controller.</li>
      <li>
        Ensure that persons authorised to process Personal Data are bound by confidentiality
        obligations.
      </li>
      <li>
        Implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect Personal Data,
        including self-hosting analytics and email infrastructure.
      </li>
      <li>
        Not engage sub-processors without prior written consent of the Controller, except for
        the sub-processors listed in Section 6.
      </li>
      <li>
        Assist the Controller in responding to data subject rights requests (access, erasure,
        portability) within a reasonable timeframe.
      </li>
      <li>
        Notify the Controller without undue delay upon becoming aware of a Personal Data breach
        that is likely to result in a risk to the rights and freedoms of natural persons.
      </li>
      <li>
        At the Controller's choice, delete or return all Personal Data upon termination of the
        services.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Sub-processors</h2>
    <p>
      Nowispow currently uses the following sub-processors. We will provide prior notice of
      changes to this list:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Sub-processor</th>
          <th>Purpose</th>
          <th>Location</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Resend</td>
          <td>Transactional email relay</td>
          <td>United States</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Lemon Squeezy</td>
          <td>Payment processing (Merchant of Record)</td>
          <td>United States</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      PostHog and Listmonk are self-hosted by Nowispow and are not third-party sub-processors.
    </p>

    <h2>7. International Data Transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Personal Data processed by Resend and Lemon Squeezy may be transferred to and stored in
      the United States. Such transfers are made under standard contractual clauses or other
      lawful transfer mechanisms as required by applicable law.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Controller Obligations</h2>
    <p>The Controller represents that it has a lawful basis to provide Personal Data to Nowispow
    and to instruct Nowispow to process it as described herein.</p>

    <h2>9. Governing Law</h2>
    <p>
      This DPA is governed by the laws of the State of Texas. For Controllers subject to GDPR
      or UK GDPR, applicable EU/UK data protection law takes precedence where it conflicts with
      Texas law with respect to data protection obligations.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      To execute a signed DPA or for data protection inquiries:
      <a href="mailto:webmaster@nowispow.com">webmaster@nowispow.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
